# ESLint is the formatter in this project, not Prettier.
#
# Everything here is formatted and enforced by `yarn lint` / `yarn lint:fix`, whose rules come
# from @jahia/eslint-config (which extends xo): semi always, single quotes, no trailing comma,
# 4-space indent, no object-curly spacing. All committed sources already satisfy them.
#
# Prettier cannot be aligned to that ruleset. It was tried: matching semi, trailingComma,
# arrowParens and bracketSpacing to the resolved ESLint config takes a spec file from 262
# violations down to 10, but two disagreements have no setting that resolves them --
#   * `indent`: Prettier and ESLint's indent rule differ on nested/chained expressions;
#   * `quotes`: Prettier emits double quotes for strings containing an apostrophe, and
#     ESLint's quotes rule here is `single` with no avoidEscape.
# The usual escape hatch (eslint-config-prettier, which switches formatting authority to
# Prettier) would relax rules this project does enforce, and leave already-committed files in a
# different style from anything Prettier later touches.
#
# So Prettier is made inert instead. This matters because nothing here ever ran it deliberately:
# no npm script invokes it, and .eslintrc.json does not extend plugin:prettier/recommended. The
# only way it ran was an editor "format on save" -- which silently reformatted a spec by 262
# lines and left `yarn lint` failing on every one of them, for a change nobody asked for.
#
# If you genuinely want Prettier to own formatting, that is a deliberate migration: add
# eslint-config-prettier to .eslintrc.json's extends, reformat every source in one commit, and
# delete this file. Do not do it by half.
*
